Why this is here:
  A pinned, offline fixture for the harness-testing walkthrough in
  docs/harness-testing.md. oh-my-claudecode is a popular (~36k★) Claude Code
  plugin that ships ALL FOUR harness surfaces in one plugin — hooks, skills,
  agents (subagents), and an MCP server — so a single example can walk every
  tier (unit → deterministic → eval) against one real plugin.

Included — the harness-relevant SLICE only, NOT the whole repo (upstream is
~117 MB / 5.7k files: a large dist/, src/, and bridge/ we do not need):
  .claude-plugin/plugin.json   — manifest, TRIMMED: the `skills` array is
                                  reduced to the two vendored skills and the
                                  `commands` key is dropped (commands/ not
                                  vendored) so the loader sees a coherent plugin
                                  with no spurious dangling refs.
  .mcp.json                    — the MCP server declaration (the 4th surface).
                                  Parsed/flagged by the loader, never executed.
  hooks/hooks.json             — TRIMMED to the single UserPromptSubmit hook
                                  whose script chain we vendored (keyword-detector).
                                  The upstream file wires ~26 scripts across 11
                                  events; we keep only the one that runs cleanly
                                  in isolation so the deterministic tier executes
                                  a REAL hook without dragging in dist/.
  scripts/run.cjs              — the hook entrypoint wrapper (node builtins only).
  scripts/keyword-detector.mjs — the UserPromptSubmit hook: detects a "magic
                                  keyword" in the prompt and injects skill-routing
                                  additionalContext. Deterministic and
                                  side-effect-free for the keyword path — verified
                                  before vendoring — so it is the one upstream hook
                                  this dogfood actually EXECUTES (unit + deterministic
                                  tiers). Its closed lib dependency set:
  scripts/lib/{atomic-write,config-dir,state-root,stdin}.mjs
  skills/{ask,verify}/SKILL.md — two representative skills.
  agents/{code-reviewer,critic}.md — two representative subagents.

Refresh: tools/refresh-vendor.sh (human-run; bumps the pinned commit).
